    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d277">

                <pb facs="0458" n="354" sameAs="frus:frus1913/pg354"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 437.00/49.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister to the Secretary of State.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Legation</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Habana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1913-03-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">March 27, 1913</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>The Cuban Congress adjourned March 26 without acting on the Guantanamo matter.
                    New Congress convenes April 6.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Beaupré</hi>.</signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Note.</hi>—The proposed treaty expired by
                        limitation June 27, 1913, since by its article 5 a stipulation was made for
                        its ratification within six months from its date: December 27, 1912. See
                            <ref target="frus:frus1912/pg_297">For. Rel. 1912, p. 297</ref>.</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
